('QM.LM1.03','quant','Normality of residuals','Q-Q plot with points on the forty five degree line through the middle and bending away at both tails.','0 0 270 170','<line class="grid" x1="26" y1="18" x2="26" y2="130"/><line class="grid" x1="26" y1="130" x2="226" y2="130"/><text class="lab" x="126" y="145" text-anchor="middle">theoretical quantile</text><text class="lab" x="10" y="74" transform="rotate(-90 10 74)" text-anchor="middle">empirical</text><line x1="26" y1="130" x2="226" y2="18" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="1" opacity=".5" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><g class="pt"><circle cx="49.5" cy="120.0" r="2.3"/><circle cx="64.5" cy="111.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="72.5" cy="105.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="78.3" cy="102.1" r="2.3"/><circle cx="82.9" cy="97.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="86.8" cy="97.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="90.3" cy="92.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="93.3" cy="91.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="96.2" cy="89.2" r="2.3"/><circle cx="98.8" cy="89.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="101.3" cy="87.2" r="2.3"/><circle cx="103.6" cy="86.5" r="2.3"/><circle cx="105.8" cy="85.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="108.0" cy="83.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="110.1" cy="83.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="112.1" cy="81.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="114.0" cy="80.0" r="2.3"/><circle cx="115.9" cy="79.5" r="2.3"/><circle cx="117.8" cy="78.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="119.7" cy="75.6" r="2.3"/><circle cx="121.5" cy="76.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="123.3" cy="76.0" r="2.3"/><circle cx="125.1" cy="74.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="126.9" cy="73.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="128.7" cy="72.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="130.5" cy="71.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="132.3" cy="68.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="134.2" cy="69.5" r="2.3"/><circle cx="136.1" cy="68.3" r="2.3"/><circle cx="138.0" cy="66.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="139.9" cy="64.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="141.9" cy="65.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="144.0" cy="64.6" r="2.3"/><circle cx="146.2" cy="60.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="148.4" cy="62.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="150.7" cy="60.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="153.2" cy="58.5" r="2.3"/><circle cx="155.8" cy="55.7" r="2.3"/><circle cx="158.7" cy="56.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="161.7" cy="56.4" r="2.3"/><circle cx="165.2" cy="51.9" r="2.3"/><circle cx="169.1" cy="50.8" r="2.3"/><circle cx="173.7" cy="48.1" r="2.3"/><circle cx="179.5" cy="41.3" r="2.3"/><circle cx="187.5" cy="37.1" r="2.3"/><circle cx="202.5" cy="28.8" r="2.3"/></g><text class="lab bad" x="224" y="30" text-anchor="end">heavy right tail</text><text class="lab bad" x="34" y="124">heavy left tail</text>','Normal residuals sit on the diagonal. Here the centre is fine and both tails bend away, so extreme residuals are larger than normality predicts. That is exactly what breaks t-tests in small samples &mdash; the middle of the distribution tells you nothing about it.',ARRAY['QM.LM1.c']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM4.01','quant','High leverage point vs outlier','Left panel: a point far to the right in X pulling the fitted line. Right panel: a point far above in Y.','0 0 560 180','<g transform="translate(24,20)"><text class="ttl" x="0" y="-6">High leverage &#8212; extreme in X</text><line class="grid" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="112"/><line class="grid" x1="0" y1="112" x2="210" y2="112"/><g class="pt"><circle cx="32.0" cy="60.7" r="2.1"/><circle cx="72.9" cy="67.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="38.6" cy="51.7" r="2.1"/><circle cx="77.2" cy="71.7" r="2.1"/><circle cx="76.3" cy="55.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="58.8" cy="55.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="86.7" cy="41.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="40.7" cy="49.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="40.8" cy="26.0" r="2.1"/><circle cx="106.7" cy="47.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="124.4" cy="57.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="53.3" cy="57.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="75.3" cy="39.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="58.5" cy="41.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="30.7" cy="54.1" r="2.1"/><circle cx="131.3" cy="60.2" r="2.1"/><circle cx="69.5" cy="63.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="73.6" cy="58.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="34.8" cy="38.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="41.1" cy="51.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="112.1" cy="49.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="126.9" cy="33.2" r="2.1"/><circle cx="108.8" cy="55.1" r="2.1"/><circle cx="105.5" cy="67.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="26.4" cy="72.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="36.7" cy="53.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="130.7" cy="49.0" r="2.1"/><circle cx="58.1" cy="62.0" r="2.1"/><circle cx="69.3" cy="77.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="60.8" cy="36.9" r="2.1"/></g><circle cx="196" cy="34" r="4" fill="var(--amber)"/><line x1="8" y1="86" x2="205" y2="30" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="1.3" opacity=".7"/><line x1="8" y1="80" x2="205" y2="52" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 3"/><text class="lab" x="0" y="130">h&#7522;&#7522; &#62; 3(k+1)/n</text></g><g transform="translate(310,20)"><text class="ttl" x="0" y="-6">Outlier &#8212; extreme in Y</text><line class="grid" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="112"/><line class="grid" x1="0" y1="112" x2="210" y2="112"/><g class="pt"><circle cx="201.2" cy="54.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="209.7" cy="54.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="38.7" cy="46.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="72.6" cy="47.1" r="2.1"/><circle cx="186.8" cy="53.4" r="2.1"/><circle cx="67.1" cy="33.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="126.2" cy="43.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="194.0" cy="61.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="148.7" cy="38.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="123.8" cy="50.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="65.2" cy="49.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="122.4" cy="39.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="197.0" cy="52.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="118.9" cy="78.6" r="2.1"/><circle cx="146.7" cy="61.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="200.9" cy="60.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="65.6" cy="51.7" r="2.1"/><circle cx="136.7" cy="77.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="29.9" cy="49.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="38.9" cy="67.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="10.3" cy="58.2" r="2.1"/><circle cx="194.3" cy="56.5" r="2.1"/><circle cx="106.3" cy="65.1" r="2.1"/><circle cx="138.8" cy="57.0" r="2.1"/><circle cx="192.5" cy="59.1" r="2.1"/><circle cx="122.3" cy="47.9" r="2.1"/><circle cx="62.4" cy="65.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="91.0" cy="62.3" r="2.1"/><circle cx="141.4" cy="59.8" r="2.1"/><circle cx="209.3" cy="56.7" r="2.1"/></g><circle cx="104" cy="12" r="4" fill="var(--red)"/><line x1="6" y1="72" x2="204" y2="44" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="1.3" opacity=".7"/><text class="lab" x="0" y="130">|t*&#7522;| &#62; critical t</text></g>','Leverage is extremity in an independent variable, an outlier is extremity in the dependent variable. Neither is automatically a problem &mdash; a high leverage point sitting on the line is harmless. It matters when the point is both extreme and off the line, which is what studentised residuals detect.',ARRAY['QM.LM4.a']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM3.02','quant','Multicollinearity signature','Left box lists the regression output pattern: insignificant t-stats with a significant F-stat and high R squared. Right box gives the variance inflation factor test and thresholds.','0 0 480 175','<rect class="node" x="20" y="22" width="200" height="118" rx="2"/><text class="ttl" x="34" y="42">Regression output says</text><text class="nt bad" x="34" y="64">&#215; t-stats insignificant</text><text class="nt bad" x="34" y="82">&#215; standard errors inflated</text><text class="nt ok" x="34" y="100">&#10003; F-stat significant</text><text class="nt ok" x="34" y="118">&#10003; R&#178; high</text><path class="edge" d="M220 81 H262" marker-end="url(#c)"/><text class="el" x="241" y="74" text-anchor="middle">contradiction</text><rect class="node-r" x="262" y="22" width="196" height="118" rx="2"/><text class="ttl" x="276" y="42">VIF diagnosis</text><text class="nt" x="276" y="64">VIF = 1 / (1 &#8722; R&#178;&#8339;)</text><text class="lab" x="276" y="82">regress each IV on the others</text><text class="nt ok" x="276" y="102">1 &#8211; 5 fine</text><text class="nt wn" x="276" y="118">&#62; 5 concerning &#183; &#62; 10 present</text><text class="lab" x="20" y="162">coefficients stay consistent &#8212; they are imprecise, not wrong</text><defs><marker id="a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--faint)"/></marker><marker id="g" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker><marker id="m" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--amber)"/></marker><marker id="c" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--cyan)"/></marker></defs>','The tell is the contradiction: individually nothing matters, jointly everything does. That combination is almost always multicollinearity. Note coefficients remain consistent &mdash; the problem is precision, so if you only need prediction it may not need fixing at all.',ARRAY['QM.LM3.d']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM4.03','quant','Why linear regression fails on a binary DV','Left: a straight line fitted to binary outcomes running above one. Right: an S-shaped logistic curve bounded between zero and one.','0 0 500 180','<g><text class="ttl" x="30" y="20">Linear probability model</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="26" x2="30" y2="118"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="118" x2="226" y2="118"/><text class="lab" x="128" y="133" text-anchor="middle">X</text><text class="lab" x="14" y="72" transform="rotate(-90 14 72)" text-anchor="middle">P(Y=1)</text><line x1="30" y1="26" x2="226" y2="26" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><text class="lab" x="24" y="30" text-anchor="end">1</text><text class="lab" x="24" y="121" text-anchor="end">0</text><line x1="36" y1="112" x2="220" y2="8" stroke="var(--red)" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="212" cy="14" r="9" fill="none" stroke="var(--red)" stroke-dasharray="3 2"/><text class="lab bad" x="206" y="36" text-anchor="end">p &#62; 1</text><circle cx="30" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="43" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="56" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="69" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="82" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="95" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="108" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="121" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="140" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="153" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="166" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="179" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="192" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="205" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="218" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/></g><g transform="translate(268,0)"><text class="ttl" x="30" y="20">Logit model</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="26" x2="30" y2="118"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="118" x2="226" y2="118"/><text class="lab" x="128" y="133" text-anchor="middle">X</text><line x1="30" y1="26" x2="226" y2="26" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><path d="M30.0 117.8 L32.8 117.7 L35.6 117.7 L38.4 117.6 L41.2 117.5 L44.0 117.5 L46.8 117.4 L49.6 117.2 L52.4 117.1 L55.2 116.9 L58.0 116.8 L60.8 116.5 L63.6 116.2 L66.4 115.9 L69.2 115.6 L72.0 115.1 L74.8 114.6 L77.6 114.0 L80.4 113.3 L83.2 112.4 L86.0 111.5 L88.8 110.3 L91.6 109.1 L94.4 107.6 L97.2 105.9 L100.0 104.0 L102.8 101.8 L105.6 99.4 L108.4 96.7 L111.2 93.8 L114.0 90.6 L116.8 87.2 L119.6 83.6 L122.4 79.8 L125.2 75.9 L128.0 72.0 L130.8 68.1 L133.6 64.2 L136.4 60.4 L139.2 56.8 L142.0 53.4 L144.8 50.2 L147.6 47.3 L150.4 44.6 L153.2 42.2 L156.0 40.0 L158.8 38.1 L161.6 36.4 L164.4 34.9 L167.2 33.7 L170.0 32.5 L172.8 31.6 L175.6 30.7 L178.4 30.0 L181.2 29.4 L184.0 28.9 L186.8 28.4 L189.6 28.1 L192.4 27.8 L195.2 27.5 L198.0 27.2 L200.8 27.1 L203.6 26.9 L206.4 26.8 L209.2 26.6 L212.0 26.5 L214.8 26.5 L217.6 26.4 L220.4 26.3 L223.2 26.3 L226.0 26.2" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="1.8" fill="none"/><circle cx="30" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="43" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="56" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="69" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="82" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="95" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="108" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="121" cy="118" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="140" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="153" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="166" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="179" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="192" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="205" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><circle cx="218" cy="26" r="2.2" class="ptc"/><text class="lab ok" x="226" y="46" text-anchor="end">bounded 0&#8211;1</text></g><text class="lab" x="30" y="166">ln[p/(1&#8722;p)] = b&#8320; + b&#8321;X &#8212; log-odds is linear, probability is not</text>','A straight line through 0/1 outcomes eventually predicts probabilities outside [0,1], which is meaningless. The logit transform makes the log-odds linear while keeping p bounded. Coefficients are estimated by maximum likelihood, not least squares, because the log-odds is undefined at p = 0 or 1.',ARRAY['QM.LM4.c']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.01','quant','Linear vs log-linear trend','Left: a straight trend line under an exponentially curving series. Right: the same series after taking natural logs, now straight.','0 0 520 175','<g><text class="ttl" x="30" y="20">Linear &#8212; constant amount</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="26" x2="30" y2="116"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="116" x2="216" y2="116"/><text class="lab" x="123" y="131" text-anchor="middle">t</text><text class="lab" x="14" y="71" transform="rotate(-90 14 71)" text-anchor="middle">y</text><path d="M30.0 105.4 L32.7 104.5 L35.3 103.6 L38.0 102.7 L40.6 101.8 L43.3 100.9 L45.9 100.0 L48.6 99.1 L51.3 98.2 L53.9 97.3 L56.6 96.4 L59.2 95.5 L61.9 94.6 L64.5 93.7 L67.2 92.8 L69.9 91.9 L72.5 91.0 L75.2 90.1 L77.8 89.1 L80.5 88.2 L83.1 87.3 L85.8 86.4 L88.5 85.5 L91.1 84.6 L93.8 83.7 L96.4 82.8 L99.1 81.9 L101.7 81.0 L104.4 80.1 L107.1 79.2 L109.7 78.3 L112.4 77.4 L115.0 76.5 L117.7 75.6 L120.3 74.7 L123.0 73.8 L125.7 72.9 L128.3 71.9 L131.0 71.0 L133.6 70.1 L136.3 69.2 L138.9 68.3 L141.6 67.4 L144.3 66.5 L146.9 65.6 L149.6 64.7 L152.2 63.8 L154.9 62.9 L157.5 62.0 L160.2 61.1 L162.9 60.2 L165.5 59.3 L168.2 58.4 L170.8 57.5 L173.5 56.6 L176.1 55.7 L178.8 54.8 L181.5 53.8 L184.1 52.9 L186.8 52.0 L189.4 51.1 L192.1 50.2 L194.7 49.3 L197.4 48.4 L200.1 47.5 L202.7 46.6 L205.4 45.7 L208.0 44.8 L210.7 43.9 L213.3 43.0 L216.0 42.1" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1.3" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="4 3"/><path d="M30.0 109.0 L32.7 108.7 L35.3 108.4 L38.0 108.1 L40.6 107.8 L43.3 107.5 L45.9 107.2 L48.6 106.9 L51.3 106.6 L53.9 106.2 L56.6 105.9 L59.2 105.5 L61.9 105.1 L64.5 104.8 L67.2 104.4 L69.9 104.0 L72.5 103.5 L75.2 103.1 L77.8 102.7 L80.5 102.2 L83.1 101.7 L85.8 101.2 L88.5 100.7 L91.1 100.2 L93.8 99.7 L96.4 99.1 L99.1 98.6 L101.7 98.0 L104.4 97.4 L107.1 96.8 L109.7 96.1 L112.4 95.5 L115.0 94.8 L117.7 94.1 L120.3 93.4 L123.0 92.6 L125.7 91.8 L128.3 91.1 L131.0 90.2 L133.6 89.4 L136.3 88.5 L138.9 87.7 L141.6 86.7 L144.3 85.8 L146.9 84.8 L14