 r="1.9"/><circle cx="215.3" cy="70.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="47.3" cy="65.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="104.9" cy="70.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="66.9" cy="72.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="207.7" cy="68.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="69.1" cy="70.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="131.8" cy="67.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="207.4" cy="69.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="67.9" cy="73.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="185.6" cy="70.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="166.7" cy="71.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="191.5" cy="72.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="178.2" cy="72.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="165.7" cy="69.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="70.8" cy="67.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="37.7" cy="72.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="103.7" cy="69.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="150.3" cy="67.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="211.6" cy="76.4" r="1.9"/></g><text class="lab ok" x="34" y="140">taking ln linearises the growth</text></g><text class="lab" x="30" y="166">if a linear trend shows DW &#8800; 2, the series is probably growing at a rate, not an amount</text>','Financial and economic series usually compound, so a linear trend systematically under- then over- then under-predicts, which shows up as serial correlation rather than as an obviously bad fit. Durbin&ndash;Watson away from 2 on a linear trend is the signal to switch to log-linear.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.a','QM.LM5.b']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.02','quant','Mean reversion','An oscillating series crossing a horizontal mean-reverting level, falling when above it and rising when below.','0 0 480 170','<line class="grid" x1="30" y1="20" x2="30" y2="120"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="120" x2="330" y2="120"/><text class="lab" x="180" y="135" text-anchor="middle">t</text><line x1="30" y1="70" x2="330" y2="70" stroke="var(--violet)" stroke-width="1.3"/><text class="lab" x="334" y="66" fill="var(--violet)">b&#8320;/(1&#8722;b&#8321;)</text><text class="lab" x="334" y="78" fill="var(--faint)">mean-reverting level</text><path d="M30 70.0 L33 66.9 L36 63.8 L39 60.8 L42 57.9 L45 55.2 L48 52.7 L51 50.4 L54 48.3 L57 46.5 L60 44.9 L63 43.7 L66 42.7 L69 42.0 L72 41.7 L75 41.7 L78 42.0 L81 42.6 L84 43.5 L87 44.6 L90 46.1 L93 47.8 L96 49.7 L99 51.9 L102 54.2 L105 56.7 L108 59.3 L111 62.0 L114 64.8 L117 67.6 L120 70.4 L123 73.2 L126 76.0 L129 78.6 L132 81.1 L135 83.5 L138 85.8 L141 87.8 L144 89.6 L147 91.2 L150 92.6 L153 93.6 L156 94.4 L159 95.0 L162 95.2 L165 95.2 L168 94.9 L171 94.4 L174 93.5 L177 92.4 L180 91.1 L183 89.5 L186 87.8 L189 85.8 L192 83.7 L195 81.5 L198 79.2 L201 76.7 L204 74.2 L207 71.7 L210 69.2 L213 66.7 L216 64.3 L219 62.0 L222 59.7 L225 57.6 L228 55.7 L231 53.9 L234 52.3 L237 50.9 L240 49.7 L243 48.8 L246 48.1 L249 47.7 L252 47.5 L255 47.5 L258 47.8 L261 48.4 L264 49.2 L267 50.2 L270 51.4 L273 52.8 L276 54.4 L279 56.2 L282 58.0 L285 60.1 L288 62.2 L291 64.3 L294 66.6 L297 68.8 L300 71.0 L303 73.2 L306 75.4 L309 77.5 L312 79.5 L315 81.3 L318 83.0 L321 84.6 L324 86.0 L327 87.2 L330 88.2" stroke="var(--cyan)" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/><path class="edge" d="M84 42 Q96 56 104 66" marker-end="url(#a)"/><text class="lab wn" x="88" y="36">above &#8594; falls</text><path class="edge" d="M160 98 Q172 84 180 74" marker-end="url(#a)"/><text class="lab ok" x="150" y="112">below &#8594; rises</text><text class="lab" x="30" y="146">every covariance-stationary series has a finite mean-reverting level; a random walk does not</text><text class="lab bad" x="30" y="160">b&#8321; = 1 makes the denominator zero &#8212; that is the unit root</text><defs><marker id="a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--faint)"/></marker><marker id="g" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker><marker id="m" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--amber)"/></marker><marker id="c" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--cyan)"/></marker></defs>','The level is b&#8320;/(1&minus;b&#8321;). The algebra carries the intuition: as b&#8321; approaches 1 the level runs off to infinity, and at exactly 1 it is undefined. That is the same condition as a unit root, which is why |b&#8321;| &lt; 1 is the stationarity requirement.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.f']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.03','quant','Random walk and first differencing','Left: a wandering random walk with no fixed level. Right: the differenced series, a stationary band of noise around zero.','0 0 520 180','<g><text class="ttl" x="30" y="18">Random walk &#8212; not stationary</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="24" x2="30" y2="124"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="124" x2="226" y2="124"/><path d="M30 76.2 L32 74.2 L34 69.5 L36 61.4 L38 67.1 L40 70.1 L42 74.0 L44 75.4 L46 76.0 L48 81.5 L50 80.3 L52 86.4 L54 84.0 L55 87.8 L57 86.4 L59 84.5 L61 84.9 L63 87.4 L65 90.7 L67 95.5 L69 88.7 L71 86.0 L73 77.7 L75 76.0 L77 74.4 L79 76.9 L81 77.9 L83 84.6 L85 80.2 L87 75.8 L89 69.2 L91 62.7 L93 67.1 L95 77.9 L97 74.5 L99 73.3 L101 77.5 L103 81.4 L104 77.8 L106 69.8 L108 67.7 L110 70.7 L112 66.9 L114 61.9 L116 67.1 L118 63.7 L120 67.9 L122 67.7 L124 65.5 L126 65.2 L128 71.7 L130 70.0 L132 76.2 L134 73.0 L136 81.4 L138 83.6 L140 85.6 L142 88.7 L144 87.7 L146 86.5 L148 78.4 L150 76.3 L152 71.4 L153 76.4 L155 71.6 L157 67.7 L159 61.6 L161 55.2 L163 59.1 L165 64.9 L167 68.3 L169 71.1 L171 64.9 L173 73.6 L175 73.4 L177 68.9 L179 69.5 L181 75.8 L183 79.7 L185 77.3 L187 74.0 L189 74.7 L191 73.1 L193 66.9 L195 68.4 L197 59.6 L199 64.0 L201 55.5 L202 61.8 L204 55.9 L206 55.8 L208 62.6 L210 62.1 L212 59.6 L214 57.0 L216 56.5 L218 57.3 L220 58.6 L222 58.2 L224 52.7" stroke="var(--red)" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/><text class="lab bad" x="30" y="140">Var(x&#8348;) = (t&#8722;1)&#963;&#178; &#8212; grows without bound</text><text class="lab" x="30" y="154">no finite mean to revert to</text></g><g transform="translate(272,0)"><text class="ttl" x="30" y="18">After first differencing</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="24" x2="30" y2="124"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="124" x2="226" y2="124"/><line x1="30" y1="74" x2="226" y2="74" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><g class="pt"><circle cx="155.3" cy="64.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="73.7" cy="72.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="174.3" cy="85.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="47.0" cy="96.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="112.7" cy="65.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="129.0" cy="72.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="35.2" cy="68.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="136.8" cy="57.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="73.2" cy="92.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="31.3" cy="85.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="187.9" cy="77.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="60.5" cy="84.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="217.6" cy="76.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="49.0" cy="69.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="196.1" cy="91.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="173.0" cy="87.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="135.1" cy="62.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="138.2" cy="76.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="192.6" cy="91.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="143.2" cy="90.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="168.1" cy="65.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="86.7" cy="71.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="45.6" cy="73.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="84.5" cy="68.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="154.6" cy="81.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="71.1" cy="65.4" r="1.9"/><circle cx="82.3" cy="58.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="149.4" cy="80.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="63.5" cy="74.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="104.4" cy="81.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="223.9" cy="83.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="164.2" cy="85.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="195.2" cy="72.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="36.3" cy="82.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="91.8" cy="74.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="214.8" cy="65.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="201.8" cy="80.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="107.5" cy="58.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="209.3" cy="83.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="78.3" cy="71.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="140.0" cy="75.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="206.0" cy="58.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="108.3" cy="66.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="129.9" cy="33.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="47.8" cy="68.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="153.0" cy="72.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="185.2" cy="77.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="104.8" cy="72.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="225.2" cy="105.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="198.7" cy="79.8" r="1.9"/><circle cx="32.3" cy="77.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="135.2" cy="91.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="82.3" cy="77.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="115.2" cy="78.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="118.9" cy="50.7" r="1.9"/><circle cx="81.6" cy="81.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="128.1" cy="62.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="200.6" cy="50.3" r="1.9"/><circle cx="88.5" cy="84.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="60.0" cy="86.5" r="1.9"/><circle cx="179.5" cy="94.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="133.9" cy="79.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="30.1" cy="75.1" r="1.9"/><circle cx="212.1" cy="71.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="202.2" cy="69.0" r="1.9"/><circle cx="41.4" cy="82.9" r="1.9"/><circle cx="202.1" cy="69.2" r="1.9"/><circle cx="125.3" cy="75.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="43.6" cy="72.6" r="1.9"/><circle cx="55.2" cy="94.2" r="1.9"/></g><text class="lab ok" x="30" y="140">&#916;x&#8348; = &#949;&#8348; &#8212; covariance stationary</text><text class="lab wn" x="30" y="154">b&#8320; = b&#8321; = 0, so no forecasting power</text></g>','Differencing rescues the statistics but not the economics. The differenced series is stationary and regression is now valid, yet both coefficients are zero &mdash; the only conclusion available is that the original series was a random walk. Passing the test is not the same as gaining a forecast.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.i','QM.LM5.j']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.04','quant','Time-series model selection','Decision flow: trend model, Durbin-Watson test, autoregressive model, stationarity check, residual autocorrelation, seasonality, then ARCH test.','0 0 700 300','<rect class="node-c" x="16" y="14" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="75" y="29" text-anchor="middle">Trend model</text><text class="nm" x="75" y="41" text-anchor="middle">linear / log-linear</text><path class="edge" d="M134 31 H176" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="176" y="14" width="112" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="232" y="29" text-anchor="middle">Durbin&#8211;Watson</text><text class="nm" x="232" y="41" text-anchor="middle">H&#8320;: DW = 2</text><path class="edge edge-y" d="M288 24 H352" marker-end="url(#g)"/><text class="el" x="320" y="18" text-anchor="middle">no SC</text><rect class="node-ok" x="352" y="8" width="96" height="30" rx="2"/><text class="nt ok" x="400" y="27" text-anchor="middle">Trend model OK</text><path class="edge edge-n" d="M232 48 V78" marker-end="url(#m)"/><text class="el" x="240" y="66">SC present</text><rect class="node-c" x="176" y="78" width="112" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="232" y="93" text-anchor="middle">AR(1)</text><text class="nm" x="232" y="105" text-anchor="middle">needs cov. stationarity</text><path class="edge" d="M176 95 H150 V152 H134" marker-end="url(#a)"/><text class="el" x="152" y="128">test first</text><rect class="node-r" x="16" y="136" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="75" y="151" text-anchor="middle">Unit root?</text><text class="nm" x="75" y="163" text-anchor="middle">Dickey&#8211;Fuller</text><path class="edge" d="M75 170 V206" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="16" y="206" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="75" y="221" text-anchor="middle">First difference</text><text class="nm" x="75" y="233" text-anchor="middle">then re-test</text><path class="edge" d="M288 95 H344" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="344" y="78" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="403" y="93" text-anchor="middle">Residual autocorr.</text><text class="nm" x="403" y="105" text-anchor="middle">any lag significant?</text><path class="edge edge-n" d="M403 112 V146 H316 V112" marker-end="url(#m)"/><text class="el" x="360" y="142" text-anchor="middle">yes &#8594; AR(2), re-test</text><path class="edge edge-y" d="M462 95 H524" marker-end="url(#g)"/><text class="el" x="493" y="89" text-anchor="middle">clean</text><rect class="node" x="524" y="78" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="583" y="93" text-anchor="middle">Seasonal lag?</text><text class="nm" x="583" y="105" text-anchor="middle">4th / 12th autocorr.</text><path class="edge" d="M583 112 V162" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="524" y="162" width="118" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="583" y="177" text-anchor="middle">Test ARCH(1)</text><text class="nm" x="583" y="189" text-anchor="middle">H&#8320;: a&#8321; = 0</text><path class="edge edge-y" d="M524 179 H486 V222 H500" marker-end="url(#g)"/><rect class="node-ok" x="500" y="206" width="76" height="30" rx="2"/><text class="nt ok" x="538" y="225" text-anchor="middle">Model OK</text><text class="el" x="482" y="196" text-anchor="end">fail to reject</text><path class="edge edge-n" d="M642 179 H672 V222 H648" marker-end="url(#m)"/><rect class="node-r" x="590" y="206" width="58" height="30" rx="2"/><text class="nt bad" x="619" y="225" text-anchor="middle">Use GLS</text><text class="el" x="676" y="196">reject</text><defs><marker id="a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--faint)"/></marker><marker id="g" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker><marker id="m" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--amber)"/></marker><marker id="c" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--cyan)"/></marker></defs>','Nearly every time-series vignette is a walk through this flow. The trap is starting at AR(1) without confirming covariance stationarity &mdash; with a unit root present the AR(1) coefficient is biased and everything downstream is invalid.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.o']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.05','quant','Seasonality and ARCH','Left: autocorrelation bars with spikes at lags four and eight. Right: a residual series with a visibly more volatile middle section.','0 0 520 185','<g><text class="ttl" x="30" y="18">Seasonal autocorrelation</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="24" x2="30" y2="120"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="120" x2="226" y2="120"/><rect class="barc" x="34" y="44.72" width="9" height="27"/><rect class="barc" x="49" y="65.84" width="9" height="6"/><rect class="barc" x="64" y="72" width="9" height="4"/><rect class="barc" x="79" y="47.8" width="9" height="24"/><rect class="barc" x="94" y="67.6" width="9" height="4"/><rect class="barc" x="109" y="72" width="9" height="2"/><rect class="barc" x="124" y="50.88" width="9" height="21"/><rect class="barc" x="139" y="68.48" width="9" height="4"/><rect class="barc" x="154" y="72" width="9" height="2"/><rect class="barc" x="169" y="53.96" width="9" height="18"/><rect class="barc" x="184" y="69.36" width="9" height="3"/><rect class="barc" x="199" y="72" width="9" height="1"/><rect class="barc" x="214" y="56.6" width="9" height="15"/><line x1="30" y1="72" x2="226" y2="72" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1"/><text class="lab" x="30" y="136">lag &#8594;  spikes at 4 (quarterly), 12 (monthly)</text><text class="lab ok" x="30" y="150">add x&#8348;&#8331;&#8324; as a regressor</text></g><g transform="translate(272,0)"><text class="ttl" x="30" y="18">ARCH &#8212; volatility clusters</text><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="24" x2="30" y2="120"/><line class="grid" x1="30" y1="120" x2="226" y2="120"/><line x1="30" y1="72" x2="226" y2="72" stroke="var(--faint)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="2 3"/><path d="M30 80.0 L32 67.2 L35 68.7 L37 75.4 L40 71.9 L42 70.2 L45 71.2 L47 71.3 L50 66.9 L52 64.1 L54 59.9 L57 72.2 L59 77.6 L62 66.9 L64 74.2 L67 78.4 L69 59.3 L72 64.9 L74 74.4 L77 74.6 L79 69.1 L81 70.4 L84 68.4 L86 72.7 L89 86.2 L91 86.9 L94 65.4 L96 70.0 L99 128.7 L101 66.6 L104 64.2 L106 53.1 L108 71.0 L111 63.7 L113 93.5 L116 115.3 L118 80.8 L121 69.6 L123 81.5 L126 113.6 L128 87.2 L130 91.7 L133 55.3 L135 103.1 L138 100.8 L140 90.7 L143 69.9 L145 43.6 L148 59.9 L150 109.1 L152 101.0 L155 34.0 L157 66.0 L160 78.2 L162 62.2 L165 56.2 L167 28.1 L170 70.2 L172 77.7 L175 79.9 L177 65.3 L179 71.9 L182 70.8 L184 68.4 L187 79.6 L189 60.1 L192 73.5 L194 73.7 L197 74.3 L199 71.1 L202 74.7 L204 74.9 L206 67.5 L209 61.9 L211 66.1 L214 80.8 L216 75.4 L219 61.6 L221 71.6 L224 71.1" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/><rect x="98" y="28" width="70" height="88" fill="var(--amber)" opacity=".07"/><text class="lab wn" x="30" y="136">&#949;&#178;&#8348; = a&#8320; + a&#8321;&#949;&#178;&#8348;&#8331;&#8321; + &#956;</text><text class="lab wn" x="30" y="150">reject a&#8321; = 0 &#8594; ARCH(1) present, use GLS</text></g>','Two different residual pathologies. Seasonality is a predictable spike at a fixed lag and is fixed by adding that lag as a regressor. ARCH is variance depending on last period''s variance &mdash; visible as calm and turbulent stretches &mdash; and needs generalised least squares.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.l','QM.LM5.m']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM5.06','quant','Regression with two time series','Three outcomes from unit root testing two series, with the both-have-a-unit-root branch leading to a cointegration test that splits into valid and spurious.','0 0 620 200','<text class="ttl" x="20" y="20">Run Dickey&#8211;Fuller on each series first</text><rect class="node-ok" x="20" y="34" width="132" height="36" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="86" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Neither has a unit root</text><text class="nm" x="86" y="62" text-anchor="middle">OLS valid</text><rect class="node-r" x="20" y="80" width="132" height="36" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="86" y="96" text-anchor="middle">One has, one does not</text><text class="nm" x="86" y="108" text-anchor="middle">coefficients inconsistent</text><rect class="node" x="20" y="126" width="132" height="36" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="86" y="142" text-anchor="middle">Both have a unit root</text><text class="nm" x="86" y="154" text-anchor="middle">depends on cointegration</text><path class="edge" d="M152 144 H196" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node-c" x="196" y="126" width="140" height="36" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="266" y="142" text-anchor="middle">Engle&#8211;Granger test</text><text class="nm" x="266" y="154" text-anchor="middle">DF on the residuals</text><path class="edge edge-y" d="M336 136 H392" marker-end="url(#g)"/><text class="el" x="364" y="130" text-anchor="middle">reject H&#8320;</text><rect class="node-ok" x="392" y="118" width="140" height="36" rx="2"/><text class="nt ok" x="462" y="134" text-anchor="middle">Cointegrated</text><text class="nm" x="462" y="146" text-anchor="middle">long-run relation, OLS ok</text><path class="edge edge-n" d="M336 154 H392" marker-end="url(#m)"/><text class="el" x="364" y="172" text-anchor="middle">fail to reject</text><rect class="node-r" x="392" y="158" width="140" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt bad" x="462" y="174" text-anchor="middle">Not cointegrated</text><text class="nm" x="462" y="186" text-anchor="middle">spurious &#8212; do not use OLS</text><text class="lab" x="20" y="182">only two of these outcomes give valid regression results</text><defs><marker id="a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--faint)"/></marker><marker id="g" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker><marker id="m" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--amber)"/></marker><marker id="c" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--cyan)"/></marker></defs>','Two unit roots is not automatically fatal &mdash; if the series are cointegrated they share a long-run relationship and OLS estimates it. If they are not, the regression is spurious: high R&#178;, significant t-stats, and no relationship at all.',ARRAY['QM.LM5.n']::text[],'generated'),
('QM.LM6.01','quant','ML algorithm map','Decision map from whether data is labelled, splitting into supervised regression and classification algorithms, unsupervised dimension reduction and clustering, and a shared group of neural and reinforcement methods.','0 0 660 240','<rect class="node-c" x="20" y="16" width="116" height="34" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="78" y="31" text-anchor="middle">Is data labelled?</text><text class="nm" x="78" y="43" text-anchor="middle">target variable present</text><path class="edge edge-y" d="M136 26 H196" marker-end="url(#g)"/><text class="el" x="166" y="20" text-anchor="middle">yes</text><path class="edge edge-n" d="M136 42 H196 V152" marker-end="url(#m)"/><text class="el" x="166" y="56" text-anchor="middle">no</text><rect class="node" x="196" y="10" width="110" height="32" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="251" y="29" text-anchor="middle">Supervised</text><path class="edge" d="M306 26 H352" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="352" y="4" width="132" height="26" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="418" y="15" text-anchor="middle">Continuous target</text><text class="nm" x="418" y="27" text-anchor="middle">regression, LASSO, CART, RF</text><path class="edge" d="M306 26 V56 H352" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="352" y="42" width="132" height="26" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="418" y="53" text-anchor="middle">Categorical target</text><text class="nm" x="418" y="65" text-anchor="middle">logit, SVM, KNN, CART</text><rect class="node" x="196" y="136" width="110" height="32" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="251" y="155" text-anchor="middle">Unsupervised</text><path class="edge" d="M306 152 H352" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="352" y="116" width="132" height="26" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="418" y="127" text-anchor="middle">Dimension reduction</text><text class="nm" x="418" y="139" text-anchor="middle">PCA</text><path class="edge" d="M306 152 V172 H352" marker-end="url(#a)"/><rect class="node" x="352" y="158" width="132" height="26" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="418" y="169" text-anchor="middle">Clustering</text><text class="nm" x="418" y="181" text-anchor="middle">k-means, hierarchical</text><rect class="node-c" x="512" y="60" width="130" height="60" rx="2"/><text class="nt" x="577" y="80" text-anchor="middle">Either target type</text><text class="nm" x="577" y="94" text-anchor="middle">neural nets, deep learning</text><text class="nm" x="577" y="107" text-anchor="middle">reinforcement learning</text><path class="edge" d="M484 17 H500 V78 H512" marker-end="url(#a)"/><path class="edge" d="M484 171 H500 V102 H512" marker-end="url(#a)"/><text class="lab" x="20" y="208">supervised = 6 algorithms &#183; unsupervised = 3 &#183; either = 3</text><text class="lab wn" x="20" y="224">the exam asks which algorithm suits a described problem &#8212; start from labelled vs not</text><defs><marker id="a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--faint)"/></marker><marker id="g" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--green)"/></marker><marker id="m" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--amber)"/></marker><marker id="c" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8 z" fill="var(--cyan)"/></marker></defs>','Nearly every ML question reduces to walking this map. Two facts about the target &mdash; is it present, and is it continuous or categorical &mdash; eliminate most of the answer choices before you consider any algorithm''s mechanics.',ARRAY['QM.LM6.a']::text[],'generated'),
